UPDATE companies SET description='Nevada Distribution & Control was founded in 1998 in Las Vegas, Nevada, by an owner who had previously worked for wholesalers. The owner opened the business to offer personal service and excellent products at lower prices, leveraging industry contacts built over years.

The company specializes in the sale of new, reconditioned, and obsolete circuit breakers, along with a range of electrical components including bus plugs, motor controls, mounting hardware, panelboard switches, and transformers. It also purchases excess inventory from industrial and commercial clients nationwide. Operations include testing and repair of electrical equipment performed by certified AVO® technicians, 24-hour emergency service, and next-day or same-day delivery via UPS, FedEx, and motor freight. The inventory comprises thousands of SKUs across major brands such as Eaton, Siemens, Square D, and Westinghouse, with no minimum or maximum order requirements. All reconditioned products carry a two-year warranty.

The company reports a customer base of over 3,000 clients.

The founder’s stated vision is to provide personal service and excellent products for less. The company emphasizes its large, ever-changing inventory, certified technicians, rapid delivery options, and a no-minimum-order policy as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sales of new circuit breakers", "Sales of reconditioned circuit breakers", "Sales of obsolete circuit breakers", "Purchase of surplus/excess electrical inventory", "Electrical testing and repair", "Equipment diagnosis", "24-hour emergency service", "Next-day delivery", "Same-day delivery", "Standard delivery (UPS, FedEx, motor freight)", "Warranty coverage (2-year on reconditioned)", "Inventory management (large, rotating stock)"], "industries": ["Industrial", "Commercial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Next-day, same-day, and standard delivery options", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Two-year warranty on all reconditioned products", "24-hour emergency service availability", "Next-day, same-day, and standard delivery options", "No minimum or maximum order requirements", "Certified AVO\u00ae technicians for testing and repair"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1998 -> /", "Headquarters in Las Vegas, Nevada -> /", "Specializes in sales of new, reconditioned, and obsolete circuit breakers -> /about-us", "Buys excess/surplus inventory from industrial and commercial clients -> /about-us", "Provides testing and repair services with certified AVO\u00ae technicians -> /about-us", "Offers 24-hour emergency services -> /about-us", "Offers next-day, same-day, and standard delivery via UPS, FedEx, motor freight -> /about-us", "Two-year warranty on all reconditioned products -> /about-us", "No minimum or maximum order -> /about-us", "Inventory includes thousands of SKUs across categories (breakers, bus plugs, motor controls, etc.) -> /", "Carries major brands: Bussmann, Cutler Hammer, Eaton, Federal Pacific, General Electric, Siemens, Square D, Westinghouse -> /", "Serves industrial and commercial clients nationwide -> /about-us", "Reports over 3,000 customers -> /about-us", "Sales staff has over 50 years combined experience -> /about-us", "Owner started business after working for wholesalers -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Nevada Distribution & Control specializes in sales of new, reconditioned, and obsolete circuit breakers, but we also provide industrial and commercial clients nationwide with the chance to sell their surplus inventory for a fair price.", "founded_year": "1998", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "No minimum order", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='nevada-distribution-control' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Nevada Precision Sheet Metal Inc. operates from Las Vegas, Nevada, serving the prototype and rapid-turn fabrication market. The company works from paper prints or electronic files and processes a full range of raw materials including steel, stainless steel, aluminum, copper, and spring steel in sheet, tube, angle, and channel forms.

The shop runs two flat laser cutters and one of Nevada''s few CNC tube lasers, a Trumpf TruLaser Tube 7000 capable of cutting diameters from 5/8 inch to 10 inches with bevels up to 45 degrees. A 7,000 psi waterjet with a 5-axis head handles sheets up to 13 by 6 feet, while high-definition plasma machines cut aluminum, stainless, and mild steel from 3 mm to 25 mm thick. Two 14-foot CNC shears hold tolerance to ±0.005 inch, and a press brake department handles bending. Welding covers MIG and TIG for ornamental to structural work. Finishing includes a 7-by-21-foot powder-coat booth and a 40 hp sand-blasting system. In-house drafters provide 3D CAD design and modeling.

Customers span medical equipment (bed frames, carts, wheelchair frames), fitness and recreational gear (exercise machines, ATV roll cages, playground equipment), food-processing tubing, industrial furniture, construction and off-road machinery, signage and store fixtures, conveyor systems, and architectural metalwork. The company also produces components for forklifts, crane supports, and material-handling racks.

NPSM emphasizes on-time delivery and a staff of experienced fabricators dedicated to quality, positioning itself as a rapid-turn partner for prototype and short-run production.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Tube laser cutting (Trumpf TruLaser Tube 7000)", "Flat laser cutting", "Waterjet cutting (7000 psi, 5-axis)", "High-definition plasma cutting", "CNC shearing", "CNC punching", "Press brake bending", "MIG/TIG welding", "Powder coating", "Sand blasting", "3D CAD design and modeling"], "industries": ["Medical equipment", "Fitness equipment", "Food processing", "Industrial furniture", "Construction equipment", "Off-road vehicles", "Signage and displays", "Store fixtures", "Material handling", "Architectural metalwork", "Recreational equipment", "Automotive components", "Conveyor systems", "Playground equipment"], "materials": ["Steel", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Copper", "Spring steel"], "equipment": ["Trumpf TruLaser Tube 7000", "7000 psi waterjet with HD-5 axis cutting head", "Two 14ft CNC shears", "Two flat laser cutting machines", "CNC tube laser", "Powder coating booth (7 ft W x 21 ft L x 7 ft H)", "40 hp screw compressor sand blasting system", "High-definition plasma cutting machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "\u00b10.005 in (shearing)", "built_on": ["Prototype and rapid-turn specialist", "On-time delivery commitment", "Full-range material capability (steel, stainless, aluminum, copper, spring steel)", "In-house 3D CAD design and modeling", "One of Nevada''s only CNC tube lasers (Trumpf TruLaser Tube 7000)"], "facts_used": ["Location: Las Vegas, Nevada -> db", "Prototype and rapid-turn market focus -> /about", "Materials: steel, stainless steel, aluminum, copper, spring steel in sheet, tube, angle, channel -> /about", "Two flat lasers and one CNC tube laser (Trumpf TruLaser Tube 7000) -> /services", "Tube laser cutting diameters 5/8\" to 10\", bevel up to 45\u00b0 -> /", "Waterjet: 7000 psi, 5-axis head, bed 13'' x 6'' -> /services", "High-definition plasma: 3mm-25mm for aluminum, stainless, mild steel -> /services", "Two 14ft CNC shears, tolerance \u00b10.005\" -> /services", "Press brake bending department -> /about", "MIG/TIG welding -> /services", "Powder coating booth 7x21x7 ft -> /about", "40 hp screw compressor sand blasting -> /about", "In-house drafters, 3D CAD design -> /services", "Industries: medical bed frames, carts, wheelchair frames -> /, /about", "Industries: exercise equipment, ATV roll cages, playground equipment -> /", "Industries: food processing tubing, industrial furniture, construction, off-road, signage, store fixtures, conveyor, architectural -> /", "On-time delivery commitment -> /about", "Experienced staff dedicated to quality -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We fabricate from paper prints or electronic files, and work with the full range of raw materials: steel, stainless steel and aluminum sheet, tube, angle and channel, copper sheet and bar; and spring steel.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='nevada-precision-sheet-metal' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='New Berlin Plastics was founded in 1975 by William Aukofer and Robert Zeman in New Berlin, Wisconsin. After relocations in 1976 and 1982, the company moved into a 100,000-square-foot facility in 1998 that serves as its headquarters and manufacturing site. In July 2001, Jeffery Held and Mark Siewert acquired the business and have since expanded its capabilities and customer base.

The company specializes in custom plastic injection molding with a focus on scientific molding practices. Its services span resin selection, design for manufacturability, mold flow analysis, tool design, program management through a proprietary process called LaunchLogic, tool transfers, and material management. Automation is integrated throughout production, and the facility runs over 100 simultaneous customer projects with a reported 98% on-time launch rate. Quality metrics cited include a 99.8% customer acceptance rate and a 2.2% internal scrap rate.

New Berlin Plastics serves OEMs across a range of sectors including automotive and transportation, healthcare and medical devices, electrical utility, power sports, water treatment, building and construction, controls, lawn and garden, industrial equipment, pet care, marine, small engine, and specialty hand and power tools. The company emphasizes start-to-finish project collaboration and value-added engineering support.

The founders and subsequent owners built the business on predictable outcomes and supply-chain reliability. Leadership states that the goal is to be a low-risk partner that delivers parts on time and within budget, backed by scientific process control and a culture of continuous improvement.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Scientific injection molding", "Molding automation", "Mold flow analysis", "Design for manufacturability (DFM)", "Resin selection", "Tool design", "Program management (LaunchLogic)", "Tool transfers", "Material management", "Design assistance", "Seminar and education services"], "industries": ["Automotive & Transportation", "Healthcare & Medical Devices", "Electrical Utility", "Specialty Hand & Power Tool", "Power Sports", "Water Treatment", "Building & Construction", "Controls", "Lawn & Garden", "Industrial", "Pet Care", "Marine", "Small Engine"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["99.8% customer acceptance rate on delivered parts", "2.2% internal scrap rate", "98% on-time launch track record across 100+ simultaneous projects", "Proprietary LaunchLogic project launch process", "Scientific injection molding with tight process control"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1975 by William Aukofer and Robert Zeman -> /about-us", "100,000 sq ft facility since 1998 -> /about-us", "Acquired July 2001 by Jeffery Held and Mark Siewert -> /about-us", "Headquarters New Berlin, Wisconsin -> /about-us", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /", "99.8% customer acceptance rate -> /", "2.2% internal scrap rate -> /", "98% on-time launch track record -> /", "100+ simultaneous open customer projects -> /", "LaunchLogic proprietary project launch process -> /", "Scientific injection molding -> /", "Molding automation -> /", "Mold flow analysis -> /", "Design for manufacturability -> /", "Tool design -> /services", "Program management -> /services", "Tool transfers -> /services", "Material management -> /services", "Resin selection -> /services", "Industries served list -> /", "Recently purchased Building 2 -> /", "50 years of partnerships -> /", "Seminars offered -> /services", "Leadership team names -> /about-us", "UL familiarity -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "New Berlin Plastics is a custom plastic injection molding manufacturer specializing in scientific injection molding, medical device components, engineered plastic parts, and precision injection molded products for OEMs throughout Wisconsin and North America.", "founded_year": "1975", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='new-berlin-plastics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='New Hampshire WoodWorks operates from Northwood, New Hampshire, where it has been crafting wooden heirlooms since 2001. The veteran-owned and operated shop began with a stock of locally harvested maple, oak, birch, and beech seasoning in a drying shed, providing the raw material for its first creations.

The company produces handcrafted items including beehives, custom tarot reading tables, nightstand bowls, and a range of unexplained underfoot objects. Each piece is shaped from wood dried on-site, with the nightstand bowls offered in varieties such as sunburst spalted maple. The workshop focuses on small-batch, heirloom-quality woodworking rather than volume production.

Customers include beekeepers seeking durable hives, tarot practitioners commissioning reading tables, and gift buyers looking for distinctive wooden bowls.

The veteran ownership informs the business''s emphasis on durability and craftsmanship, with the drying shed and local lumber sourcing cited as foundations for the quality of each finished piece.', certifications=ARRAY['VETERAN OWNED']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Woodworking", "Wood seasoning/drying", "Custom woodworking", "Heirloom furniture making", "Beehive construction", "Tarot table fabrication", "Bowl turning", "Spalted maple working"], "industries": ["Consumer goods", "Giftware", "Beekeeping equipment", "Metaphysical supplies", "Custom woodworking"], "materials": ["Maple", "Oak", "Birch", "Beech", "Spalted maple"], "equipment": ["Drying shed"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Veteran owned and operated", "Locally harvested maple, oak, birch, and beech", "On-site wood seasoning in drying shed", "Handcrafted heirloom-quality construction", "Custom tarot tables and nightstand bowls"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2001 -> db", "Veteran owned & operated -> db, /", "Headquarters Northwood, New Hampshire -> db", "Products: beehives, tarot tables, nightstand bowls, custom portfolio, unexplained underfoot objects -> /", "Materials: locally harvested maple, oak, birch, beech -> /", "Wood seasoned in drying shed -> /", "Sunburst spalted maple bowls -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "CRAFTING QUALITY SINCE 2001. VETERAN OWNED & OPERATED", "founded_year": "2001", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Veteran-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='new-hampshire-woodworks' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='New Jersey Semiconductor Products Inc. was established in 1957 and is headquartered in Springfield, New Jersey. The company operates from a two-story, 50,000-square-foot facility in Springfield, where it has built a reputation for producing highly reliable discrete devices over more than six decades.

The company designs and manufactures high-reliability discrete semiconductor devices, including Zener diodes, rectifiers, field-effect transistors (FETs), transient voltage suppressors (TVS), unijunctions, bridge rectifiers, and European-type devices. It maintains an extensive inventory of both current-production and end-of-life components, supported by on-site engineering and technical support.

Its products serve military, avionics, industrial, and commercial markets worldwide. Customers include engineers and manufacturers who require stable supply and responsive technical support for demanding applications.

The company differentiates itself through a library of current and obsolete devices, a just-in-time delivery program, and same-day or short-lead-time shipping on most stocked items. These capabilities stem from decades of experience and a focus on consistent electrical performance and long-term dependability.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Discrete semiconductor design", "Discrete semiconductor manufacturing", "Zener diode production", "Rectifier production", "FET production", "TVS production", "Unijunction production", "Bridge rectifier production", "European-type semiconductor production", "Engineering and technical support", "Just-in-time delivery", "End-of-life device sourcing"], "industries": ["Military", "Avionics", "Industrial", "Commercial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day and short lead time delivery on most items", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day and short-lead-time delivery on most stocked items", "Just-in-time delivery program", "Library of current-production and end-of-life devices", "On-site engineering and technical support", "Over 50 years of discrete semiconductor manufacturing experience"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1957 -> /about", "Headquartered in Springfield, New Jersey -> /about, db", "Two-story 50,000-square-foot facility -> /about", "Serves military, avionics, industrial, and commercial markets -> /about", "Specializes in Zener diodes, rectifiers, FETs, TVS, unijunctions, bridges, European types -> /about", "On-site engineering and technical support -> /about", "Just-in-time delivery program -> /about", "Same-day and short lead time delivery on most items -> /about", "Library of current-production and end-of-life devices -> /about", "Designs and manufactures high-reliability discrete semiconductor solutions -> /", "Products include transient voltage suppressors, rectifiers, switching transistors, custom replacements -> /", "Decades of industry experience and rig