UPDATE companies SET description='New Process Fibre Company, Inc. has operated from Greenwood, Delaware since its founding in 1927. The business remains family-owned, describing itself as a family business committed to improving products, maximizing quality, and maintaining cost-effectiveness.

The company manufactures non-metallic washers, spacers, gaskets, shims, and custom shapes through stamping and plastic extrusion. All processes run under one roof: the firm extrudes its own thermoplastics, maintains an in-house tool room with wire EDM for custom tooling, and uses CAD/CAM for design. Services include slitting, shearing, and precision die cutting of materials such as PTFE, nylon, vulcanized fibre, Lexan, phenolic, acetal, G-10 FR4, and UHMW.

Customers span aerospace and military, appliances, automotive, electronics, HVAC, power tools, medical, and plumbing sectors. Named references include Flotec, which uses NPF parts for oxygen manifold systems in field hospitals; Tesla; the University of Calgary; Mueller Die; Klinger IGI; Knife & Gun Finishing Supplies; and Derby Fabricating Solutions.

It offers free maintenance of tool designs for the life of a program with a partial tooling charge, and its hard tooling, developed in-house, enables tighter production tolerances. The company also provides material selection guides and technical resources for engineers.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ROHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Non-Metallic Stamping", "Plastic Extrusion", "Slitting", "Shearing", "Wire EDM Tooling", "CAD/CAM", "Custom Die Cutting", "Washer Manufacturing", "Spacer Manufacturing", "Gasket Manufacturing", "Shim Manufacturing", "Custom Shape Stamping", "Thermoplastic Extrusion", "Material Selection Guidance"], "industries": ["Aerospace & Military", "Appliances", "Automotive", "Electronics", "HVAC", "Power Tools", "Medical", "Plumbing"], "materials": ["Teflon/PTFE", "Nylon", "Vulcanized Fibre", "Lexan", "Phenolic", "Acetal (Delrin)", "G-10 FR4", "Mylar", "Polyethylene", "Polypropylene", "UHMW"], "equipment": ["Wire EDM"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house tool room with wire EDM for custom tooling", "Extrusion of own thermoplastics", "Free tool design maintenance for life of program", "Hard tooling for tighter production tolerances", "Family-owned since 1927"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1927 -> db", "Headquarters Greenwood, Delaware -> db", "Family-owned business -> homepage", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> homepage", "ROHS compliant -> db", "In-house tool room with wire EDM -> homepage", "Extrudes own thermoplastics -> homepage", "CAD/CAM capabilities -> homepage", "Serves aerospace, military, automotive, electronics, HVAC, medical, plumbing, appliances, power tools -> homepage", "Customers include Flotec, Tesla, University of Calgary, Mueller Die, Klinger IGI, Knife & Gun Finishing Supplies, Derby Fabricating Solutions -> homepage", "Free tool design maintenance for life of program -> homepage", "Hard tooling for tighter tolerances -> homepage", "Materials: PTFE, Nylon, Vulcanized Fibre, Lexan, Phenolic, Acetal, G-10 FR4, Mylar, Polyethylene, Polypropylene, UHMW -> homepage"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Custom Manufacturer of top-quality washers and components made from Teflon\u2122/PTFE, Nylon, Vulcanized Fibre, Lexan, Phenolic, and MANY other plastics and stamping materials.", "founded_year": "1927", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='new-process-fibre-company-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='New York Custom Interior Millwork Corp. was founded in 1972 by Teddy Lagos, who opened a retail woodworking shop on Fifth Avenue in Manhattan. The family-owned business later expanded to a showroom and manufacturing plant in Long Island City before establishing its headquarters in Astoria, Queens. John’s University and working alongside her father. She now runs the company with her father serving as a mentor and consultant.

The firm produces custom architectural millwork for high-end commercial and residential projects. Its capabilities span in-house design, fabrication, finishing, and installation, all performed in a state-of-the-art facility. The company works with wood as well as a range of non-wood architectural materials, offering complete turnkey solutions from concept through final fit-out.

Primary clients include architects, interior designers, real estate developers, and construction managers. The portfolio references work in stadiums, broadcast studios, luxury hotels, and five-star restaurants across the United States and internationally.

