UPDATE companies SET description='New York Metal Fabricator operates from New York City, serving the five boroughs and surrounding areas. The company describes itself as locally owned and operated, with over 20 years of industry experience. No founding year or founder names are disclosed.

The shop provides full-service metal fabrication and welding, working with steel, aluminum, copper, brass, bronze, wrought iron, and stainless steel. Capabilities include custom metal fabrication, structural steel fabrication (beams, columns, frames, trusses), architectural metalwork (facades, canopies, panels), custom railings and staircases, and NYC DOT-compliant outdoor dining structures for restaurants and bars. Processes cover cutting, bending, MIG, TIG, and stick welding, both in-shop and mobile, followed by finishing and quality inspection of welds, dimensions, and surface finishes. The company also offers consultation, design with 3D modeling, fabrication, and installation.

Customers span residential, commercial, and industrial sectors. Architects, designers, and property owners commission decorative and structural pieces, while hospitality clients have received dozens of code-compliant outdoor dining structures since the city legalized curbside dining in 2020.

The firm emphasizes quality, experience, and personal service, citing fast turnarounds without compromising quality, competitive pricing, free estimates, and certified welding that meets code requirements.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom metal fabrication", "Structural steel fabrication", "Architectural metalwork", "Metal railings and staircases fabrication", "Outdoor dining structure fabrication", "MIG welding", "TIG welding", "Stick welding", "Mobile welding", "In-shop welding", "Metal cutting", "Metal bending", "Metal finishing", "Design consultation", "3D modeling", "Installation services", "Quality inspection"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Architectural", "Hospitality", "Property management"], "materials": ["Steel", "Brass", "Bronze", "Aluminum", "Copper", "Wrought iron", "Stainless steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 20 years of industry experience", "Full-service metal fabrication and welding under one roof", "NYC DOT-compliant outdoor dining structures delivered since 2020", "Certified MIG, TIG, and stick welding with mobile and in-shop options", "End-to-end process from consultation and 3D design through installation and quality assurance"], "facts_used": ["Located in New York City -> db", "Over 20 years of industry experience -> /", "Locally owned and operated -> /", "Services: custom metal fabrication, structural steel, architectural metalwork, railings/staircases, outdoor dining structures -> /", "Materials: steel, aluminum, copper, brass, bronze, wrought iron, stainless steel -> /", "Processes: cutting, bending, MIG/TIG/stick welding, mobile and in-shop, finishing, quality inspection -> /", "Industries: residential, commercial, industrial, architects, designers, property owners, restaurants/bars -> /", "NYC DOT-compliant outdoor dining structures since 2020 -> /", "End-to-end process: consultation, 3D design, fabrication, installation, quality assurance -> /", "Referral website disclaimer: leads sent to JA VISUALS INC. -> /services"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "unclear", "type_evidence": "Please note that this is a customer referral website, with all leads sent to JA VISUALS INC.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='new-york-metal-fabricator' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='New York Woodwork operates from a workshop in Brooklyn, New York, where it was founded in 1997 with the goal of designing and handcrafting custom cabinetry for discerning clients.

The firm designs, manufactures, and installs custom cabinets, countertops, kitchen islands, bathroom vanities, walk-in closets, built-in furniture, and media centers. Its Brooklyn facility handles custom wood finishes including paint, thermofoil, Formica, stain, and lacquer. Beyond fabrication, the company provides end-to-end project management that covers demolition, reconstruction, and coordination of trades such as plumbing and electrical. It also supplies ready-made cabinetry that can be customized to specific dimensions for architects and builders ordering in bulk.

Clients range from individual homeowners and apartment residents to multi-unit condominiums and commercial developers. Notable projects have included work for the NYPD, major department stores, restaurants, hospitals, hair salons, and hotels across the East Coast. The company frequently collaborates with architects and designers who require detailed millwork for residential and commercial spaces.

New York Woodwork emphasizes a dedicated project manager for every job, custom wood-grain matching, and a free design consultation either in its showroom or by phone. The company states that its proposals include detailed costs for both design and production, and that typical kitchen or bathroom renovations take three to six months, excluding structural changes requiring permits.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cabinetry design", "Custom woodworking manufacturing", "Installation of cabinets and millwork", "Project management (demolition to installation)", "Custom wood finishes (paint, thermofoil, Formica, stain, lacquer)", "Custom furniture and built-ins fabrication", "Kitchen island fabrication (fixed and mobile)", "Bathroom cabinetry fabrication", "Walk-in closet systems", "Countertop fabrication", "Shelving and media center fabrication", "Home office built-ins", "Ready-made cabinetry customization", "Architect and builder collaboration", "Trade coordination (plumbing, electrical, HVAC)", "Demolition and removal", "Reconstruction and remodeling"], "industries": ["Residential (homeowners, apartments)", "Multi-unit condominiums", "Commercial development", "Hospitality (restaurants, hotels)", "Healthcare (hospitals)", "Retail (department stores, hair salons)", "Government (NYPD)", "Architecture and design firms"], "materials": ["Wood", "Paint", "Thermofoil", "Formica", "Stain", "Lacquer", "Hardware"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "3 to 6 months for kitchen or bathroom renovation (excluding structural changes)", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["End-to-end solutions from demolition through installation", "Dedicated project manager oversees every phase of the project", "Custom wood-grain matching to existing interiors", "Ready-made cabinetry customized to dimensions for bulk orders", "Free design consultation in showroom or by phone"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1997 -> /about", "Headquartered in Brooklyn, NY -> /, /abo