oHS -> db, /about", "Standards: IPC-WHMA-A-620 Class II/III, UL 508A -> /about", "Redundant capabilities, three-hour drive service radius -> /about", "24-hour response, 5-day quote -> /, /about", "Bill of materials scrubbing, secure storage, dedicated inventory -> /", "Quality system, vendor audits, continuous improvement -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Since 1997, we have manufactured high-complexity circuit board assemblies \u2014 and built lasting customer partnerships.", "founded_year": "1997", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='niche-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Niehoff Endex North America operates from Swedesboro, New Jersey, serving as the North American arm of a global machinery builder. The business traces its roots through Endex, which was part of Bekaert Corporation in Lakewood, New Jersey until 1999. The company states it brings more than 25 years of experience to the wire and cable sector, though a specific founding year for the current entity is not disclosed.

The company designs and builds wire drawing machines and complete drawing lines for cable production. Its product range also includes continuous lead extruder machines for cable stripping. Beyond equipment supply, Niehoff Endex delivers turnkey projects and a full-service portfolio organized under commissioning, operation, support, and modernization programs. Spare parts are stocked and supplied as original components. Facility size, headcount, and annual output figures are not published.

Customers span the wire and cable industry broadly, with noted focus on telecommunications, electronics, automotive, and power cable manufacturers. The firm positions itself as a partner for both capital investments and after-sales support, addressing needs from new line installation to productivity improvements on existing assets.

Niehoff Endex emphasizes a "comprehensive service program" as its differentiator, combining engineering, commissioning, ongoing operational support, and modernization to extend machine life. The company describes its approach as developing products and producing solutions to keep customers "in good hands," framing reliability and long-term partnership as core to its offering.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wire drawing machine manufacturing", "Drawing line manufacturing", "Continuous lead extruder machine manufacturing", "Cable stripping equipment", "Turnkey project execution", "Commissioning services", "Operation support services", "Technical support services", "Modernization and retrofit services", "Spare parts supply"], "industries": ["Wire and cable", "Telecommunications", "Electronics", "Automotive", "Power cables"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Wire drawing machines", "Drawing lines", "Continuous lead extruder machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Comprehensive service program covering commissioning, operation, support, modernization, and spare parts", "Turnkey project capabilities for wire and cable production lines", "Modernization services to extend machine service life", "Original spare parts supply for all equipment", "More than 25 years of experience in the wire and cable industry"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Swedesboro, New Jersey -> db", "Manufacturer of wire drawing machines and drawing lines -> db", "Continuous lead extruder machines for cable stripping -> db", "Turnkey projects and modernization services -> db", "Service portfolio: commissioning, operation, support, modernization, spare parts -> db", "Industries: wire and cable, telecommunications, electronics, automotive, power cables -> db", "Endex part of Bekaert Corporation in Lakewood, NJ until 1999 -> db", "More than 25 years of experience in wire and cable industry -> db", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "NIEHOFF is one of the world''s leading manufacturers and suppliers of wire drawing machines and drawing lines for the wire and cable industry.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/niehoff-endex-na/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='niehoff-endex-north-america' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Nimbletronics, LLC was founded in 2006 in Plano, Texas, by Chester Nguyen and Cuong Nguyen. Both owners brought decades of electronics manufacturing experience from prior roles at companies such as NVIDIA, Creative Labs, Hitachi Semiconductor, and through multiple acquisitions of Texas Prototypes, TXP, Asymblix, and Circuitronics. The company emerged from a core team that had worked together since 2006, surviving three acquisitions before establishing Nimbletronics as an independent contract manufacturer.

The company provides electronics manufacturing services with a focus on quick-turn printed circuit board assembly for low-volume, high-mix orders. Its 20-foot-ceiling, humidity-controlled facility in the Dallas/Fort Worth Metroplex’s Research/Technology Crossroads district houses two SMT lines equipped with Juki pick-and-place machines, Heller nitrogen reflow ovens, EKRA screen printers, and automated optical and X-ray inspection. Processes cover surface-mount placement down to 0.20 mm pitch (including 01005 and 0201 components), through-hole, rework, clean and no-clean chemistries, and both RoHS lead-free and tin-lead soldering. Additional services include top-level mechanical assembly, cabling, flying-probe test (via partner), turnkey procurement, DFM feedback, and PCB layout and design. The shop handles prototypes, revision re-spins, alpha and beta builds, and low-to-mid-volume production with turn times ranging from same-day to 25 days.

Nimbletronics serves engineers and OEMs across semiconductor, medical, telecommunications, defense, security, audio, video, industrial, energy, radio-frequency, and network markets. Customers typically require rapid iteration on complex designs, such as fine-pitch BGAs, chip-scale packages, stacked die, and rigid-flex circuits.

The founders created Nimbletronics to build a “family-like, yet professional” culture that prioritizes on-time delivery and quality without bureaucracy. The team’s continuity through prior acquisitions is cited as proof of its ability to adapt quickly to changing customer demands, and the company’s mission is to provide a dynamic environment that turns engineers’ visions into reality on schedule.', certifications=ARRAY['RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Quick-turn PCB assembly", "Surface Mount Technology (SMT)", "Through-hole assembly", "Rework and repair", "Clean and no-clean processes", "RoHS (lead-free) and tin-lead soldering", "Fine-pitch placement (0.20 mm pitch, 01005, 0201, 0301)", "Stacked capacitor assembly", "Wafer-level and WLCSP/CSP assembly", "Flip chip and stacked CSP", "uBGA, BGA, Package on Package (PoP)", "QFP, TSSOP, SOP, SOT, DPAK placement", "Leadless packages (QFN, XDFN, MLP, TDFN, DFN, VQFN)", "Top-level mechanical assembly", "Cabling and wiring harness assembly", "Flying probe test (outsourced partner)", "Turnkey procurement and supply chain management", "DFM feedback and design review", "PCB layout and design services", "Flex and rigid-flex circuit assembly", "Backplane assembly"], "industries": ["Semiconductor", "Medical", "Telecommunications", "Defense", "Security", "Audio", "Video", "Industrial", "Energy", "Radio Frequency (RF)", "Network"], "materials": ["FR-4", "Polyimide (flex)", "Rigid-flex", "HASL", "ENIG", "OSP", "Immersion Silver (ImAg)", "Immersion Tin"], "equipment": ["Screen Printer Juki G-Titan with 2-D Solder Paste Inspection", "Pick and Place Juki 2050RE (two units)", "Pick and Place Juki 2060RE", "Juki TR6 Matrix Tray Changer", "Reflow Oven Heller 1809EXL \u2013 9 Heating + 2 Cooling Zones + Nitrogen", "Screen Printer EKRA X5 with 2 \u00bd-D Solder Paste Inspection", "Pick and Place Juki 2050RL (two units)", "Pick and Place Juki 2060RL", "Juki TR6 Matrix Tray Changer (second line)", "Reflow Oven Heller 1809EXL \u201