UPDATE companies SET description='North Dakota Soybean Processors (NDSP) operates a soybean crushing facility in Casselton, North Dakota. The company was formed as a joint venture between CGB Enterprises, Inc., a private U.S. grain and transportation company with a 50-year history, and Minnesota Soybean Processors (MnSP), a cooperative processor. The partnership was established to create a local, year-round market for soybeans grown in Cass County and the surrounding Red River Valley, adding value to the region’s harvest and stimulating the local economy.

NDSP processes soybeans into three primary products: food-grade soybean oil, soybean meal for livestock feed, and soyhull pellets. The plant is described as a state-of-the-art facility designed to serve both food and fuel markets, with the oil directed toward food users and the renewable diesel sector, while the meal supports the livestock industry. The company also offers producers a blended portfolio of pricing tools and contract options to manage market risk.

The facility serves soybean growers across North Dakota and western Minnesota, providing a reliable outlet for their crops. Its customer base includes food manufacturers, renewable fuel producers, and livestock operations that require consistent, high-quality meal and oil.

