UPDATE companies SET description='O''Neal Manufacturing Services (OMS), headquartered in Vestavia Hills, Alabama, operates as part of O''Neal Industries, a metals manufacturing network active since 1921. The company runs a dedicated structural steel fabrication plant in Fayette, Alabama, equipped with a robotic beam line, plasma and saw cutting, and paint finishing capabilities.

OMS provides integrated metal fabrication services for global OEMs across ten North American facilities. Its capabilities span heavy steel fabrication, precision welding, complex CNC machining, 5-axis laser cutting, and advanced automation, supporting multi-stage processing from initial cutting through tertiary fabrication. The network offers specialized steel sourcing and scalable production for high-volume repetitive parts and heavy-duty welded assemblies.

The company serves industries including power generation, data centers, construction, material handling, transportation, and renewable energy. Its customer base consists of Tier 1 OEMs in heavy equipment and infrastructure markets, with manufacturing locations in Cedar Falls, Iowa; Cincinnati, Ohio; Fayette, Alabama; Greensboro, North Carolina; Houston, Texas; Indianapolis, Indiana; Kingsport, Tennessee; Louisville, Kentucky; Monterrey, Mexico; and Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.

OMS differentiates itself through centralized supply chain management, providing a single point of contact for multi-step metal processing across its North American network. The company emphasizes proactive risk management, leveraging a century of manufacturing stability to ensure quality production and on-time delivery, while prioritizing technical repeatability and structural integrity.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Structural steel fabrication", "Heavy steel fabrication", "Precision welding", "Complex CNC machining", "5-axis laser cutting", "Robotic beam line processing", "Plasma cutting", "Saw cutting", "Paint finishing", "Powder coating", "Kitting and assembly", "Multi-site manufacturing coordination", "Supply chain management", "Steel sourcing"], "industries": ["Power Generation", "Data Centers", "Construction", "Material Handling", "Transportation", "Renewable Energy"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Robotic beam line", "Plasma cutting equipment", "Saw cutting equipment", "5-axis laser machining technology", "Paint finishing line", "Powder coating line"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Centralized multi-site manufacturing with a single point of contact", "Ten North American fabrication facilities", "Advanced automation including robotic beam line, plasma and saw cutting", "Proactive risk management for quality and on-time delivery", "Integrated manufacturing from cutting to complex tertiary fabrication"], "facts_used": ["Company name and headquarters -> db", "Part of O''Neal Industries active since 1921 -> db", "Structural and heavy steel fabricator with Fayette, AL plant -> db", "Robotic beam line, plasma and saw cutting, paint finishing -> db", "ISO 9001 certification -> db", "Headquartered in Birmingham, AL with ten North American facilities -> /", "Integrated services: heavy steel fabrication, precision welding, complex CNC machining, advanced automation -> /", "Industries: Power G