UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Norman, Oklahoma, Off Grid Enterprises, LLC provides design and installation services for renewable energy systems. The company''s project manager, Pieter Huebner, is a NABCEP-certified installer with thirty years of experience in the field, including a long tenure as lead installer and trainer at Bergey Wind Power from 1984 to 2013. Sheila Huebner is also noted as a key contact for the business.

Off Grid designs, builds, and installs both off-grid and grid-tied solar and wind power systems for residential, commercial, and agricultural customers. Installations range from ground-mounted and roof-mounted arrays to pergola and carport configurations. The firm also assists with energy-efficient home upgrades such as LED lighting, efficient appliances, and radiant floor heating. All equipment used is sourced from U.S. manufacturers, and the company provides ongoing maintenance and warranty coverage for its installations.

The company serves customers across a wide geography, with completed projects documented from Belize and Canada to Maine and Alaska. Typical clients include homeowners seeking to eliminate electric bills, remote-site operators needing reliable power, and agricultural operations. Off Grid holds a Texas Electrical Contractor license (No. 31460) and offers free site surveys to assess project feasibility.

The business emphasizes the importance of certified installation, noting that its NABCEP-qualified lead installer ensures compliance with electrical codes and industry standards. By using U.S.-made components and providing maintenance and warranty support, Off Grid positions itself as a full-service partner rather than a simple equipment reseller.', certifications=ARRAY['NABCEP Certified Installer','Texas Electrical Contractor License 31460']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar system design", "Solar system installation", "Off-grid power system design", "Grid-tied solar installation", "Ground-mounted solar installation", "Roof-mounted solar installation", "Pergola solar installation", "Carport solar installation", "Wind power system integration", "Generator integration with renewable systems", "Energy-efficient home design consulting", "LED lighting installation", "Energy-efficient appliance installation", "Radiant floor heating installation", "Site survey and assessment", "Maintenance and repair services", "Warranty administration", "Electrical contracting (Texas licensed)"], "industries": ["Renewable energy systems", "Solar energy", "Wind energy", "Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Agricultural", "Remote power systems", "Energy efficiency"], "materials": ["US-made solar panels", "Wind turbines", "LED lighting", "Energy-efficient appliances", "Radiant floor heating components"], "equipment": ["Bergey 10kW wind turbine"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["NABCEP-certified lead installer with 30 years of experience", "U.S.-manufactured equipment used in all installations", "Maintenance and warranty coverage included", "Free site survey for prospective customers", "Texas Electrical Contractor license (No. 31460)"], "facts_used": ["Company name, city, state, industries_served -> db", "Designs, builds, installs off-grid and grid-tied renewable energy systems -> /", "NABCEP lead installer Pieter Huebner with 30 years experience, Bergey Wind Power 1984-2013 -> /", "Sheila Huebner mentioned as contact -> /", "Installations from Belize to Canada, Maine to Alaska -> /", "Ground mounted, roof mounted, pergola, carport solar systems -> /", "Energy efficient home design: LEDs, appliances, radiant floor heating -> /", "Products made in USA, maintenance and warranty -> /", "Free site survey -> /", "Texas Electrical Contractor License 31460 -> /", "Federal tax credit mention -> /", "Testimonials referencing Pieter and Sheila -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Off Grid designs, builds, and installs off-grid and grid-tied renewable energy systems for residential, commercial, and remote areas.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='off-grid-enterprises-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Off-Grid Power Systems is based in Delaware, Ohio. The company designs and installs custom off-grid solar power systems for a range of applications. While its founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed, the business is operated by a team that includes Ed and Vinh, who are frequently cited by clients for their technical expertise and hands-on involvement in projects.

The company’s core offering is the design, supply, and installation of complete off-grid power systems. It provides pre-wired cabin kits that feature inverter load balancing and pre-wired PV protection and disconnects, eliminating the need for customers to perform component selection and compatibility verification. Off-Grid Power Systems also sells individual components such as inverters, batteries, solar charge controllers, and monitoring solutions, and integrates products from brands like Victron and Pytes. The firm handles projects from initial consultation through commissioning, including custom system design, equipment sourcing, and on-site installation.

Off-Grid Power Systems serves three primary markets: commercial installations, recreational vehicles, and off-grid properties. Commercial clients include businesses seeking green energy solutions for operations. Recreational customers encompass RV owners, conversion van builders, horse trailer operators, food truck owners, and specialty vehicle operators. The properties segment covers cabins, cottages, outbuildings, and other remote dwellings. The company has also completed projects for marine applications, such as a boat installation referenced in client feedback.

The company differentiates itself through a consultative design process that begins with a discussion of the client’s goals and needs, followed by multiple design options. It emphasizes expertise with Victron equipment and offers free consultations. Client testimonials highlight the team’s attention to detail, safety-focused installations, and ongoing support after commissioning.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom off-grid power system design", "Off-grid system installation", "Pre-wired cabin kit assembly", "Component selection and compatibility verification", "System commissioning and startup", "Sales of inverters, batteries, solar charge controllers, monitoring solutions", "Victron product integration", "Pytes battery integration", "Free consultation", "Post-installation support and training"], "industries": ["Commercial", "Recreational vehicles (RVs, conversion vans, horse trailers, food trucks, specialty vehicles)", "Off-grid residential (cabins, cottages, outbuildings)", "Marine", "Renewable energy"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Pre-wired cabin kits with inverter load balancing and PV protection", "Custom design process starting with client goals and needs", "Free consultation for all projects", "Specialized expertise with Victron energy products", "Post-installation support and system education"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Delaware, Ohio -> db", "Designs and installs custom off-grid solar power systems -> page /", "Offers pre-wired cabin kits with inverter load balancing and pre-wired PV protection -> page /", "Sells inverters, batteries, solar charge controllers, monitoring solutions -> page /", "Serves commercial, recreational (RVs, vans, trailers, food trucks), properties (cabins, cottages), marine -> page /", "Key personnel: Ed and Vinh -> page /", "Provides free consultation -> page /", "Custom design process discussing goals and needs -> page /", "Expertise with Victron products -> page /", "Offers Pytes V5\u00b0 48V 100Ah battery -> page /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "unclear", "type_evidence": "We can design and build a system that meets your specific desires.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='off-grid-power-systems' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ogonek Custom Hardwoods operates a sawmill in Barberton, Ohio, serving the Northeast Ohio region. The business grew from a family’s connection to the area, with Dan Ogonek the operation. While the exact founding year is not publicly stated, the company describes its origin as growing out of a family’s love for a place that represents more than an investment.

The sawmill specializes in custom cutting beams and timbers for timber-frame construction and home-improvement projects, including decorative beams and mantels. It can produce lengths up to 52 feet in species native to Northeast Ohio such as white pine, red oak, aspen, white oak, cherry, and black walnut. Offerings include rough-cut, non-kiln-dried material, tongue-and-groove milling, specialty blocking and dunnage, planing and ripping dimensional lumber, live-edge milling, hand-hewn beams, and installation of decorative beams.

Customers range from timber-frame builders and owner-builders to contractors renovating historic homes. Testimonials cite a cabin rebuild in Illinois and Wisconsin using 6×10 pine timbers 20 feet long, a hand-built timber-frame pavilion with planed white pine and tongue-and-groove decking, and decorative beam installation in an 1800s farmhouse. The company also supplies rough-sawn, planed, and live-edge material for various custom woodworking projects.

Ogonek emphasizes sustainably sourced local lumber and hands-on expertise; Dan Ogonek is noted for providing timber-framing suggestions drawn from experience. The crew’s focus on pride in workmanship, from wood selection to joinery, is highlighted in customer feedback as a distinguishing trait.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom beam and timber cutting", "Tongue and groove milling", "Specialty blocking and dunnage", "Planing and ripping dimensional lumber", "Live edge milling", "Hand hewing beams", "Decorative beam installation"], "industries": ["Timber framing", "Home improvement", "Custom woodworking", "Residential construction", "Historic renovation"], "materials": ["White Pine", "Red Oak", "Aspen", "White Oak", "Cherry", "Black Walnut"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom cutting up to 52-foot lengths", "Native Northeast Ohio species", "Sustainably sourced locally", "Rough-cut, non-kiln-dried material", "Timber framing expertise and on-site installation"], "facts_used": ["Located in Barberton, Ohio -> /", "Sawmill specializing in custom cutting beams and timbers -> /", "Maximum cut length 52 feet -> /", "Species: White Pine, Red Oak, Aspen, White Oak, Cherry, Black Walnut -> /", "Sustainably sourced in Northeast Ohio -> /", "Rough-cut, non-kiln-dried material -> /", "Offers tongue and groove, specialty blocking/dunnage, planing, ripping, live edge, hand hewn beams -> /", "Provides installation of decorative beams -> /", "Founder Dan Ogonek mentioned in testimonials -> /", "Family origin described in blog -> /", "Customer examples: cabin rebuild, timber frame pavilion, farmhouse decorative beams -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a sawmill with special expertise in custom cutting beams and timbers for your timber frame or other home improvement project including decorative beams and mantels.", "founded_year": "", "employee_c